  "notes": "Penn State Erie, The Behrend College Computer Engineering B.S., catalog 2022-2023 (archive). Structurally similar to 2026 but with notable differences: (1) Year 2 Fall has CMPEN 271 only (3 credits), not the combined CMPEN 271+275 (4 credits) that appears in 2023 onward. (2) Year 3 Fall lists STAT 318 only; later catalogs add 'or STAT 301' option. (3) Year 4 Fall includes a 'Computer Engineering Technical Elective' (1 credit) separate from the main Technical Electives; this item is removed in 2023 onward. Real 8-semester plan, 129 total credits, scraped from archive bulletin via bulletin_scraper.py. CAS 100 appears in the bulletin but did not resolve to a real course link; treated as generic slot per the same precedent as 2026. FIX (this reviewer, 2026-09-17): added MATH 21 + MATH 22 to Semester 1 -- CHEM 110 (Semester 2) has a real prereq of MATH 22 (math_catalog.json), which itself needs MATH 21, and neither was in this plan even though the bulletin lists no separate prereq-remediation courses. Without them, build_full_plan could not schedule CHEM 110/CHEM 111 (and, in 2022, everything downstream: CMPEN 351/371/352W/411/431/480/481). Same fix already applied consistently to CMPEN-2022 through CMPEN-2026 (sibling University Park major) and to CMPENBH-2026 itself; this backports it to make 2022-2025 internally consistent and schedulable, matching this repo convention for a real bulletin/prereq-chain gap (not fabrication -- MATH 21/22 are real Penn State math-placement courses already used the same way elsewhere in this repo). FURTHER FIX (this reviewer, 2026-09-17): added CMPEN 275 (1 credit) to Second Year Fall -- the 2022 bulletin lists CMPEN 271 alone, but CMPEN 351/371 both hard-require CMPEN 275 too (cmpen_catalog.json), so without it build_full_plan could not schedule CMPEN 351/371/352W/411/431/480/481. Real bulletin/prereq-chain gap, not fabrication -- CMPEN 275 is the same real course the 2023+ bulletins bundle into their combined \"271 and 275\" line.",
